RTM_results/
experiments/
# ANCHORED (fixed 2026-08-01) -- these two MUST keep their leading slash.
# An unanchored `data/` / `models/` matches a directory NAME AT ANY DEPTH, so it
# also excluded the SOURCE packages code/python/netdrift/{data,models}/. Those
# were therefore never committed, and a fresh clone of this repo cannot import
# netdrift.runner.run at all ("No module named 'netdrift.data'") -- which is
# exactly how it failed on the Lamarr cluster. The leading slash restricts each
# pattern to the repo root, which is what was intended: the root-level
# checkpoint tree and dataset tree.
# Same trap as the mutagen ignore rules (see mutagen_netdrift.sh) -- this repo
# has source packages named after its data directories.
/data/
/models/
results_comb/
runs*/
wandb/
docs/
weekend_*.log
*.log
logs/

nohup.out

cluster-ids*

Dockerfile
.dockerignore

.Identifier

# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*$py.class
